{"episodes":{"209942":"A strong winter storm from Sunday, February 15th into Friday, February 19th brought heavy snow, rain, and gusty winds. This brought from 1 to 7 inches of rain, with totals of around 5 to 9 feet of heavy snow above 5000 feet, 1 to 4 feet from 3500 feet to 5000 feet, and 1 to 12 inches from 500 feet to 3000 feet. ||Gusty southerly wind gusts of 25 to 50 mph in the Valley, 40 to 60 mph in the mountains and foothills were recorded. Roads were reported to be flooded, as well as covered with mud and rocks in some mountain and foothill areas. Numerous downed trees were reported during this time, along with mountain highway closures and chain restrictions, with roadway flooding in the Central Valley. Numerous roads were closed from flooding and storm damage in the Valley. Up to 80,000 power outages were reported across the mountain and foothill areas from Butte County down to Tuolumne County for an extended period. There were numerous school closures in the mountains and foothills from the storm. Water storage and pump stations were also impacted, leaving homes without water for an extended period.","210734":"Heavy rains led to river flooding on the Cache River at Patterson during the mid to late part of February.","211215":"A very powerful winter storm brought heavy rain, strong thunderstorms and gusty winds to Southwestern California Rainfall totals generally ranged from 1.50 to 4.00 inches across coastal and valley areas with 3.00 to 7.00 inches across the foothills and mountains with significant snowfall at the higher elevations. With this rainfall, numerous reports of flash flooding were received. Strong thunderstorms were also observed, resulting in strong outflow winds and wind damage.","211219":"A waterspout was reported off the coast of El Segundo.","211336":"A line of thunderstorms moving southeasterly produced a strong wind gusts at Cape Canaveral.","211417":"A series of low pressure systems moved over southern California during the mid part of the month of February, bringing heavy rain and thunderstorms, strong and gusty winds, and high elevation snow from the 10th thru the 11th, and then again on the 16th thru 18th. This resulted in a few reports of damage due to strong winds from thunderstorms. There were also several reports of flooding/flash flooding due to heavy rain."},"events":[{"begin":"2026-02-16T02:25Z","county":"Volusia-Brevard County Line To Sebastian Inlet 0-20Nm","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-02-16T02:25Z","endLat":28.53,"endLon":-80.77,"episode":211336,"id":1320304,"injuries":0,"lat":28.53,"location":"1.51 SSE Playalinda Beach","lon":-80.77,"magnitude":34.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","narrative":"USSF wind sensor on tower 0100 measured a peak wind gust of 34 knots from the southwest.","source":"Other Federal Agency","state":"Atlantic South","type":"Marine Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"MLB"},{"begin":"2026-02-16T10:58Z","county":"Butte","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-02-17T02:58Z","endLat":39.7338,"endLon":-121.831,"episode":209942,"id":1309592,"injuries":0,"lat":39.7,"location":"2.14 SSW Mullberry","lon":-121.79,"narrative":"California Highway Patrol reported roadway flooding at Lone Star Road and Hahn Road and Old Highway 99 from Delevan to Maxwell Road.","source":"Law Enforcement","state":"CA","type":"Flood","wfo":"STO"},{"begin":"2026-02-16T11:14Z","county":"San Joaquin","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-02-17T02:14Z","endLat":37.9511,"endLon":-121.2898,"episode":209942,"id":1309593,"injuries":0,"lat":37.9483,"location":"1.58 SSE Stockton","lon":-121.2908,"narrative":"California Highway Patrol reported flooding in the slow lane.","source":"Law Enforcement","state":"CA","type":"Flood","wfo":"STO"},{"begin":"2026-02-16T13:10Z","county":"Santa Barbara","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-02-16T13:10Z","endLat":34.5668,"endLon":-120.499,"episode":211